    "type": "question",
    "label": "30",
    "prompt": "Which term of $54,\\ 18,\\ 6,\\ldots$ is $\\dfrac{2}{243}$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "9th term.",
      "worked": "$a=54,\\quad r=\\dfrac13$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}a_n&=ar^{n-1}\\\\\\frac{2}{243}&=54\\left(\\frac13\\right)^{n-1}\\\\\\frac{1}{6561}&=\\left(\\frac13\\right)^{n-1}\\\\\\frac{1}{3^8}&=\\left(\\frac13\\right)^{n-1}\\\\n-1&=8\\\\n&=9\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, it is the 9th term.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
